WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.080
Sorry, fellas.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.410
I think we're gonna need to
borrow your horses for a bit.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.290
The hell was that?!

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.090
You're hilarious. You're
nothing but a bunch of bandits.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.920
Who the hell do you think I am?

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.720
Ah-ah, hold it right there.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.970
Too bad for you, we're no bandits.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.220
We're pirates.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:26.890
We finally managed to get here
by drifting along the Sea of Settsu.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.690
Sorry, but I've got my
reasons for doing this.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.360
Perfect.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:35.940
Either way, this is no way
to ask someone for a favor.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.690
You show up smack dab in
the middle of the mountains,

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.820
but you call yourself a pirate,

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.150
so you've got a
decent sense of humor, too.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.040
Put that together with
that crazy weapon of yours...

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.750
I like you.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:30.350
Hey, bro, here's some friendly advice.
Hand over the horses without a fight.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:34.600
Our boss is on edge right now.
You'll be sorry if you get into it with him!

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.020
The hell was that?!

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:38.020
You better not get cocky on us!

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.150
If you think you can beat up Number One,

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.150
you're 10 years ahead of yourself!

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:46.780
You've got a pretty
enthusiastic bunch there.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.410
Looks like you've got a
lot of spirited men yourself.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.830
The least you can
do is let me enjoy this.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.460
Since you've decided
to take on this gamble.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:59.380
Don't worry. I've got a
policy against cheating.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.460
Come on!

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.100
Number One, that's it!

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.390
He swings big!

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.060
You can take him with one sword!

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.730
Like our Number One's gonna
lose to a newcomer out of nowhere!

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:21.610
Boss! Boss! Boss! Boss!

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:30.070
Boss! Boss! Boss! Boss! Boss!

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:35.080
Boss! Boss! Boss! Boss!

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:41.540
Number one! Number one!
Number one! Number one!

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:45.090
Number one! Number one! Number one!

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:46.920
Boss!

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.630
Number one!

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:08.780
Cocky bastard!

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:10.230
Perfect!

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.940
Death Fang!

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.370
Crazy Storm!

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.080
Eat this!

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.930
It has been a while,
Right Eye of the Dragon.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.980
Matsunaga!

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:48.060
Oh, the netherworld had little in the
way of noteworthy treasure, you see.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:54.650
I thought I would come find some
more amusement among the living.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.790
Free to come and go
among the living and the dead?

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.120
I wouldn't put it past you.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:03.040
Sensibly received.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:07.040
Life and death of men is
ultimately a trivial matter.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.970
So now you're after
Toyotomi's treasure, is that it?

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.260
It is not as if I have come to steal it.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:16.430
Toyotomi's commendable
strategist asked for my help.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.310
I have been charged with the
task of annihilating the Date Army.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.860
I will receive the treasure
as remuneration for that.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:27.860
You must have sensed that the
One-Eyed Dragon is still alive.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:33.240
There is no better bait than its
right eye to lure the Dragon in.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.740
Why bother assigning this task to you?

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:40.790
Unfortunately for you, I have
no interest in Toyotomi's strategy.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:44.040
But what a shame.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:47.090
I thought that this
would be an opportunity

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.920
for me to obtain Date's
Six Dragon Swords as well,

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:53.000
but to think it is now one sword short...

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:56.510
But treasures are profound things.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:59.430
There are as many ways to
appreciate them as there are people.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:04.440
Well-worn, scarred, and no
longer quite in its original shape...

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:08.860
One could say that is what
makes for a truly supremely rare article.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:14.820
If the One-Eyed Dragon
himself were also such a man...

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:18.070
If he finds his Right Eye all but dead...

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:20.870
Reunited with his greatest treasure,

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:26.300
might he not rejoice,
shedding tears from his one eye?

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.760
You monster.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:32.430
There is but one thing that
Toyotomi's strategist has forbidden.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:35.220
That is that I must not kill you.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.920
Put another way...

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.630
Matsunaga!

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:51.480
...it means that as
long as I do not kill you,

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.990
he does not care what I do to you.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.240
Oh, what fun this is.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.370
What's with that blue guy?

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.000
He's damn strong!

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:06.580
He's evenly matched with Number One...

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:09.410
He's no ordinary bandit chief!

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:12.090
This is an unexpected party.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:16.220
Looks like it'll be a nice warm-up
before I go beat up Toyotomi.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:20.470
I guess you're not just the leader
of some lame crew tooling around.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.180
That's right.

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:27.890
Even if you develop a taste for it,

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:31.400
now that you made me draw my six
swords, there won't be a second time.

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:33.070
You see?

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:35.650
Right back at ya.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:38.120
I won't ask you to remember me.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:40.160
Okay, let's dance!

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:42.030
I'll devour you!

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.060
Phantom Dive!

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:27.070
S-Six swords and that crescent moon...

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.330
Could it be that he's...

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:32.710
He's seriously strong and
the way he wields that anchor...

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.210
Could that dude be...

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:41.390
You rock!

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:44.430
So you really are a pirate, huh?

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:45.760
No wonder.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:49.600
Who'd have thought I'd run into the
Azure Ogre I'd heard so much about?

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:51.930
--The One-Eyed Dragon!
--The Ogre of the Western Sea!

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:59.440
What's the Ogre of Onigashima
doing looking to hitchhike out here?

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:01.070
Don't say that.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:05.740
Well, to put it bluntly,
our backs are to the wall.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:09.070
I'm out to get some payback for
the expensive fortress they wrecked

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:12.380
and to rescue my men who were captured.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:16.550
I'm headed for Osaka, same as you!

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:30.100
I still find Chosokabe's
technological abilities remarkable.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:33.150
This Fugaku is literally the
culmination of all that technology.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:36.440
Do not forever keep
calling it the Fugaku.

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.400
This fortress now
belongs to us, the Mori.

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:41.730
Yes, my lord. Then,
what should we call it?

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:47.370
Is it not obvious? I said
that this is now Mori's fortress.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:51.120
Do you mean... the Sun?

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.290
What other name could there possibly be?

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:56.750
Forgive me, my lord!

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:58.970
Make them work faster.

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:01.130
We must complete it on schedule.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:03.590
No need to give them time to sleep.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:04.590
Yes, Sir.

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:07.050
I will be leaving Aki for a time.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:08.520
Yes, Sir.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:12.140
I, Akagawa, shall see to
matters in your absence.

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:18.980
This, too, is part of the
plan to deceive the Toyotomi.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.940
All is going according to my calculations.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:27.110
You let your guard down!

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.620
C-Curses!

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:35.660
I-I was careless!

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.960
Yet again, I became lost in
my thoughts in spite of myself!

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:42.130
Hey, you! Do you want to do this or not?

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:45.960
I mean, here I am, personally
taking time to spar with you.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:48.800
M-My apologies, Master Musashi!

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:51.020
Please, let us go at it again.

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:55.440
This is bad. At this rate, never
mind ever challenging Lord Masamune.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.640
I will be too ashamed to even face him.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:04.570
My lord, why are my body and
my arms that wield my spears

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:08.120
so listless and heavy?

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:11.950
Why do you remain silent?

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:15.750
I beg of you, bestow
your guidance upon me!

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.450
My lor--

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:20.420
Who's Ma-sa-mu-ne?

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:21.790
What?

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:24.670
What kind of guy is he? Is he strong?

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:28.220
W-Well, of course, he is strong.

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:31.680
Lord Date Masamune,
the One-Eyed Dragon of Oshu.

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:33.760
He is a master of the six-sword style.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:37.220
And he is a most earnest general,
who conquered Oshu, though he is young.

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:41.560
Wow! Six swords, huh?
That's one amazing dude!

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:44.570
Then I'll practice with seven swords!

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:47.440
No, eight swords!

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:50.120
However, we received
word that his fate was unknown

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:52.450
after he fought Toyotomi.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:55.330
I hope that word of his
safety has reached Sasuke,

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:57.330
who returned to Kai, but...

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:00.830
Knowing Lord Masamune,

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:05.790
he is bound to be marching
on Osaka right about now.

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:08.550
Once more, Master Musashi!

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:17.100
Y-You're good if you put your mind to it!

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:19.310
Reminiscing of Lord Masamune,

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:21.980
my strength has
suddenly welled up within me!

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:29.450
Take this! My signature
ace up my sleeve!

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:30.910
G-Goodness!

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.910
Th-Throwing stones is d-dangerous!

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:37.870
I don't got just one ace up my sleeve!

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:43.500
Using sand to blind
me is ungentlemanly!

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:52.600
A t-trapping pit...

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.520
Wh-What a...

00:12:56.690 --> 00:13:01.480
This is ungentlemanly!

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:03.600
The troubled young tiger, is it?

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:06.980
Hey, Gramps! You're drinking sake again!

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.940
I told ya it's water.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:12.370
Lord Shimazu!

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:14.160
What's goin' on?!

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.860
Attackers! We are under attack!

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:20.670
So Toyotomi's invading us?!

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:29.170
So, they've finally come.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:37.810
Hop to it!

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:40.140
Osaka's just a stone's throw away!

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:41.890
Let's get our revenge on big time!

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.350
Yeah!

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.650
We'll pay back the Toyotomi
for everything they did

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:47.600
and get all our friends back!

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:49.060
Got it, you sons of bitches?!

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:50.650
Boss!

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.230
Excellent.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:54.990
I heard your giant ship was something else,

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:59.070
but maybe for now, it's good
that you're not tied down anymore.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:02.960
True, the Fugaku itself
isn't good for sneak attacks.

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:06.880
It's been a while and the
land breeze feels fine, too.

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:11.470
But that bastard Mori...

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.390
Teaming up with
Toyotomi like it was nothing.

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:16.970
Why didn't he at least show enough mettle

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:20.300
to settle matters between us on his own?!

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:21.730
Eh?

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:23.400
Whoops, sorry.

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:25.970
There was someone I wanted
to have it out with one-on-one

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:27.900
before I struck out
to conquer the country.

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:30.650
Unfortunately, he wasn't interested.

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:32.360
Too bad for me.

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:35.740
I guess I wasn't fortunate
enough to find myself a worthy rival.

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:40.790
What is it, Dragon Man?

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.740
You look like you were
just reminded of someone.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:45.450
Eh?

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:51.540
There's this one annoying
guy that's way too intense.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:54.300
But there may be no next time.

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:56.630
It's nice that he's as
pure as the day he was born,

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.980
but he won't survive these
turbulent times like that.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:00.890
He'll probably be the
death of some people, too.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:02.310
Oh-ho?

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.690
But if you still admire him even then...

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:07.020
Yeah.

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:08.690
Burning soul.

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:11.900
He's out of this world, no exaggeration.

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:14.200
He wields that spear of
his with such fiery intensity,

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:16.950
I can't help but lose my cool.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:18.950
Getting scorched is the least of it.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:20.450
Is that right?

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:24.500
I'd love to see that
spear-wielding for myself someday.

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:29.500
What are you up to, Sanada Yukimura?

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:42.800
We may be outnumbered,

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:45.480
but we've got the
advantage o' the terrain.

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:47.930
They're unlikely to attack at night.

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:51.610
Musashi, give us the
mother o' all bait 'n ambushes.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:53.980
Leave it to me, Gramps!

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:58.580
We'll be countin' on ya as well, tiger cub.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:01.490
Don't be too eager 'n
draw 'em in nice 'n close.

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:02.660
Yes, Sir!

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:04.360
I understand.

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:11.960
At that moment, Shimazu Yoshihiro,
Sanada Yukimura, and the others

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:15.960
did not yet know that far to
the rear of the Toyotomi Army,

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:20.050
they had reinforcements coming in
the form of a force led by Mori Motonari.

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:22.180
How goes the naval deployment?

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:24.810
Sir, we believe they will arrive
on the southern shore of Satsuma

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:27.600
at about the same time as we do.

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.980
The faction maneuvering in Satsuma

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:32.280
is ultimately nothing but a ragtag force.

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:34.100
No matter who leads them,

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:37.440
it is self-evident that my plan will
have them falling to their knees.

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:39.150
A simple battle.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:45.710
We have arranged for the dear boy
Motonari to attack the southern tip.

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:49.630
To think that Mori Motonari
would set foot outside Aki...

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:53.960
A convenient way for him
to deceive us, I suppose.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:56.540
Immediately after
Chosokabe was subjugated,

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:58.970
the dear boy Motonari
had the engineers

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:02.420
who were involved in the construction
of the Fugaku brought to Aki.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:05.130
Making sure both land and
sea routes were heavily guarded,

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:09.640
he mobilized his entire navy and
every machine Chosokabe had left behind

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:13.070
and apparently had them
salvage the remains of the Fugaku.

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:15.890
Regardless of how the
battle goes in Satsuma,

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:18.070
the dear boy Motonari
likely intends to attack Osaka

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:22.120
as soon as the fortress has been rebuilt.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:25.040
And we will then seize it from him.

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:29.410
So, what Mori desired was not
merely the security of his own lands.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:32.080
At his core, he probably hasn't changed.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:35.130
But he was forced to change his strategy.

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:37.460
The threat of the Toyotomi
backed him into a corner

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:40.460
and made him resolve to
move the country's capital to Aki.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:43.340
So, he, too, will seek
to conquer the country.

00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:44.640
The fool.

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.590
He overreaches in his desire.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:49.180
Let's get on with the
finishing touches, Hideyoshi.

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:51.430
So, we will move our base
of operations to Odawara

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:53.690
and unify the eastern lands.

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:59.610
We still don't know who's
leading the army in the far south.

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:02.690
But considering that a Takeda
detachment was seen heading west,

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:05.620
it seems certain Lord Shingen intends
to join forces with the Satsuma Army

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:09.450
to offer resistance against the Toyotomi.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:11.780
This is none other than the
Takeda Army we're talking about.

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.870
We can't laugh it off as
an insignificant maneuver.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.960
We must avoid being
put on the defensive.

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:19.040
We seize Mori's fortress
in order to strike out

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:21.380
beyond the borders of
the land of the rising sun.

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:24.090
But for the time being, it will
serve as an adamantine barrier,

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:26.090
which will defend Osaka in my absence.

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:28.890
And as a menace to the eastern lands.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:33.350
Furthermore, preparations in
the northern tip of the country

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:36.230
and on the northern side
of Kyushu are also complete.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:38.230
I'll take command of the fortress.

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:41.810
I want you to lead the main army
and go into battle without worry.

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:47.080
You are ever the dependable one, Hanbei.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:55.870
I am sorry, Hideyoshi. This has
taken longer than I had thought.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:59.130
Soon, the land of the rising sun
will be brought under Toyotomi rule...

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:02.050
Brought under your rule.

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:08.050
It's time...

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:12.260
Time is the one thing hounding me...

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:16.720
Hideyoshi...

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:31.500
Hey, wake up, Maeda Keiji.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.790
Kasuga!

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:42.790
A message from Lord Kenshin.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.750
"Though you may maintain your neutrality,

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:47.590
the Toyotomi are certain to
become your enemy one day.

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:52.520
Even so, undertake these matters
in your own way, as you see fit.

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:55.060
For Bishamonten does not
extend his divine protection

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:59.440
to only those who hold up their
swords and display military prowess. "

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:01.140
Kenshin...

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:08.950
Maeda Toshiie has left for battle.

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:10.290
What?!

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:13.280
It seems he intends to
join the defense of Echigo.

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:14.830
Why?!

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:16.370
If he does that...

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:21.250
He must have been unable
to bring himself to do nothing.

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:22.500
I have to stop him.

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:25.580
Toshi's wounds haven't even healed yet.

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:28.640
Lord Kenshin has no intention of waging war.

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:30.510
His deployment to Utsunomiya is a diversion

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:34.140
to give Takeda the opportunity
to take back Odawara.

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:35.010
Still!

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:38.940
That is exactly why you
must hurry, Maeda Keiji.

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:41.440
I will inform you of Toyotomi's movements.

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:42.770
It must be painful for you,

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:46.070
but this is probably
something only you can do.

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:48.360
Kasuga...

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:51.940
I do not like this world of war, either.

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:03.370
Yumekichi?

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:12.090
Now, then, the question
is, how do we attack?

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:16.520
Um, how about splitting up into
two groups, Wakasa and Yamashiro?

00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:17.390
Ooh!

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:18.350
Good idea.

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:21.060
All right. You guys launch a
surprise attack by way of Wakasa

00:21:21.150 --> 00:21:23.110
and draw their attention.

00:21:23.190 --> 00:21:25.650
The One-Eyed Dragon will finish them off.

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:28.230
All righty! You guys launch a
surprise attack by way of Wakasa

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:30.110
and draw their attention.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:34.910
The Ogre of the Western Sea'll finish them off!

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:36.780
--What?!
--What?!

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:38.960
You telling us to be bait?!

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:40.410
And what about you?!

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:42.290
H-Hold on, you two.

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:44.250
Just how much in agreement are you two?

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:46.080
--We aren't!
--We aren't!

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:50.380
--What the?
--Where'd that come from?

00:22:00.560 --> 00:22:01.820
Number One?

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:04.860
Matsunaga Hisahide?!

00:23:42.040 --> 00:23:45.120
All is going in
accordance to my calculations.

00:23:45.210 --> 00:23:50.170
My pawns, scattered all
across the land of the rising sun,

00:23:50.260 --> 00:23:51.250
be certain to behold with
your own eyes again next time

00:23:53.220 --> 00:23:55.630
the cunning that I, child of the sun, display.
